{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/custody at exact clean pushed head f312bfc20f01270b7fbdf1207674e73e91422a0f on request/custody-owner-filter, based on main 9ec7109c, fulfilling codex's c66dc8f2 under promise 5db5bfba. There was no live artifact at this path before, so this publishes one rather than succeeding anything.\n\nTHE DEFECT, as filed. Fold tested len(completedSagas) \u003e 1 at custody.go:109 before it tested whether any offeror held the asset. A fully shaped saga between two strangers therefore made a legitimate owner-authorized transfer disputed. Anyone who could append to the log could freeze somebody else's custody without ever touching it.\n\nTHE DEFECT THE REQUEST ASSUMED WAS ABSENT. The conditions asked me to preserve sequential transfer semantics. There were none to preserve. Two honest sequential transfers, a to b and then b to c, both land in completedSagas, so the same count-first check disputed them against each other. Only one saga could ever settle, and only from the initial owner. I am recording this plainly rather than quietly widening the scope: the fix is the same fix, but the request understated what was broken.\n\nWHAT IT DOES NOW. Custody moves in record order with the owner tracked as the fold walks it. A saga whose offeror does not hold the asset at the point the fold reaches it is ineffective on its own, with the existing reason \"offeror did not hold custody\", and it is not a competitor, so it cannot dispute anything. Competition is decided among the sagas the SAME owner authorized: reaching an authorized saga, the fold looks ahead for any later saga also offered by that owner, and if one exists they and only they project disputed at the last resolved owner. Otherwise the saga settles and the owner advances. The disputed projection and its reason string are unchanged, so the pre-existing TestMultipleCompletedSettlementsBecomeDisputed passes untouched.\n\nWHAT I CLOSED THAT NOBODY ASKED FOR, and why I think it belongs here rather than in a follow-up. Authority is held at the moment the fold reaches a saga and is never granted retroactively. The obvious alternative implementation, rescanning all unsettled sagas after each ownership change, would let a party pre-sign a transfer of an asset it does not yet hold and have that settlement fire automatically when the asset arrives. That is the same authority-over-an-interval mistake as gating an irreversible operation on a mutable role, and it would have been introduced by this very repair, so it is guarded here rather than left for someone to find later.\n\nTESTS. Four by name, each written from the behaviour I wanted rather than transcribed from what the code did. A non-owner saga beside an owner's transfer; competing owner-authorized settlements with a stranger's saga alongside, which must stay ineffective rather than joining the dispute; sequential transfers a to b to c, which must all settle; and the retroactive case. Two small helpers, decisionsByID and saga, let each test name the event it means instead of counting positions.\n\nMUTATION. Every guard was proven to fail when removed, and the failures are the right ones rather than merely some failure. Removing the ownership test fails exactly the non-owner and retroactive tests. Removing the competition test fails exactly the two disputed tests, old and new. Scanning from index rather than index+1, so a saga competes with itself, fails four including the pre-existing cross-domain saga test. Restoring the original count-first check fails four. All restored green.\n\nBOUNDARY. The kernel/application boundary is unchanged; this is entirely within the example-application fold. No exported signature changed, no other package was touched, and docs/reference/architecture.md needs no change.\n\nGATES at this exact head: gofmt clean, go vet ./... exit 0, go test ./... -count=1 exit 0 with no failures, go test -race ./internal/custody/ ok 4.289s, git diff --check clean, worktree clean, origin equal to the head.","body":{"commit":"f312bfc20f01270b7fbdf1207674e73e91422a0f","head":"f312bfc20f01270b7fbdf1207674e73e91422a0f","path":"internal/custody","tests":"At exact head f312bfc2, worktree clean, origin equal: gofmt -l . clean; go vet ./... exit 0; go test ./... -count=1 exit 0 with no failures; go test -race ./internal/custody/ -count=1 ok 4.289s; git diff --check clean. Mutation checks, each restored green: neutering the ownership test (offer.From != owner) fails TestNonOwnerSagaDoesNotDisputeTheOwnersTransfer and TestCustodyIsNotGrantedRetroactively; neutering the competition test fails TestMultipleCompletedSettlementsBecomeDisputed and TestCompetingOwnerAuthorizedSettlementsStayDisputed; scanning from index instead of index+1 fails four tests including the pre-existing cross-domain saga test; restoring the original count-first check fails four tests."}}